      "slot": "the justification",
      "desc": "Rubric for the written justification. A full-credit answer says that if the coefficients are real then complex roots must come in conjugate pairs, so the partner of four minus i is four plus i. Accept a justification built by construction instead: multiplying out the two factors is the only way the imaginary parts cancel and leave real coefficients, and a student who shows the middle term becoming minus eight x has demonstrated it. No credit for asserting the pair rule with no reason attached.",
